WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:02.210
- Thank you for having me here tonight.

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:06.713
My name's Chelsea Handler and
I am as white as they come.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.420
I'm filming a documentary,
as you may or may not know

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:12.933
about white privilege.

00:00:15.995 --> 00:00:16.828
- Oh.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.430
- I'm clearly the beneficiary
of white privilege.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.500
I want to know how to
be a better white person

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.920
to people of color.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.940
We need to talk to people
who are white and stop asking

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.000
black people to solve our problems.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.050
Do you think it exists?

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.670
- I wouldn't say it's totally nonexistent

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.100
but it's not something
that I see very commonly.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.050
- But would you see it if you're white?

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.580
I got caught with dime bags on
me with my boyfriend Tyshawn

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.300
three times and every times
and every time he was arrested

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.430
and I was let go.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.700
It never occurred to me
that it was a racial thing.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.220
I shoulda known better.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.970
- To us it's so hard for a black person

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.049
than it is for a white person.

00:00:58.049 --> 00:01:00.670
(soulful music)

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:01.970
- You guys know where you come from.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:02.990
You know your history.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:03.940
We don't know that.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.840
We still don't know if we were
related to kings or queens,

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.150
or if we were farmers, or if
we built houses, we don't know.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.702
You guys know, that's a
privilege you guys have.

00:01:13.702 --> 00:01:16.030
♪ Focus your pain ♪

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:18.530
- White people have to
have the conversation

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.206
with white people.

00:01:20.206 --> 00:01:23.003
And so those are hard conversations.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.367
- It's like talking about
porn at the dinner table.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.920
(laughs)

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.753
You know.

00:01:28.753 --> 00:01:30.780
I mean, obviously at my dinner
table that would be fine but.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:31.863
- Lord have mercy.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.700
- You do need to learn about others

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.800
but you also have to learn about yourself.

00:01:41.087 --> 00:01:42.643
- Here I come white people.

00:01:43.951 --> 00:01:46.618
(soulful music)

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.430
- It's great to talk about it

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:51.560
because you need to start somewhere.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.843
But this rabbit hold goes deep.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.703
Deeper than a documentary.

